From 34d90545195c25e4884b6ae3bfb8ba5930e4cd79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Josep Torra <n770galaxy@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:29:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 34/46] drm/gma500: recover sgxfive from hung transfer jobs

A faulting transfer stalls the 3D pipe, so its job and every job after it,
on any context, never complete. Recover from the scheduler's timeout. The
firmware runs one transfer at a time, so a timeout is a hang only when the
oldest job given to the firmware is unfinished and is the same as at the
previous timeout; completions do not count, because dummy jobs still
complete while the pipe is stalled. Then the context owning that job is
lost and its unfinished jobs fail with -EIO. The firmware is reset in place,
and every other context's client CCB is rewritten with its unfinished
commands, which each hardware fence now keeps a copy of, and kicked again
once the firmware is up. The handler does the reset itself under the device
lock, which run_job now also holds for the CCB write and the kick, and
returns NO_HANG so the timed-out job stays with the scheduler and is freed
when its fence signals. Before, the job was never freed and its context
leaked. The debugfs reset node runs the same recovery without blame.

Assisted-by: LLM
